    "caveats": [
      "Ground-truth burst/stable labels are DERIVED, not an authoritative pre-existing field: burst = keys named as burst_key_id in a cold_burst drift event; stable = top-200 keys by total request frequency ...",
      "The 'fixed_reconstructed' threshold variant (CV<0.5=stable, CV>1.5=burst) is a RECONSTRUCTED approximation -- the prior experiment's exact original thresholds and window-alignment convention could not...",
      "The decision-point CV/MAD-mean statistic uses the LAST `window` inter-arrival gaps per key (mimicking a live shadow-queue classifier with only past data available at decision time)."
    ],
